WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.734
-Guys, finally,
we have exactly one show left

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:04.767
before we go on Christmas break,
which means it's time for

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:06.400
that beloved
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.000
It's time for
"12 Days of Christmas Sweaters."

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.634
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:12.968
-♪ 12 Days
of Christmas Sweaters ♪

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:17.567
♪ One day left ♪

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:20.767
-That's right!
For each of the last 12 shows

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:23.501
before Christmas, we've been
giving one lucky audience member

00:00:23.501 --> 00:00:25.200
a magnificent Christmas sweater

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.934
from the
Countdown to Christmas Cabinet.

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:31.901
So since there is one show left,
let's open door number 1.

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:33.601
Where are we?

00:00:33.601 --> 00:00:35.033
-It's right over there.
-Here?

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:36.033
-Right here.

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:37.234
-Go for it, pal.
Ready?

00:00:37.234 --> 00:00:39.267
[ Drumroll ]

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:40.400
Whoa!

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:46.000
♪♪

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.200
[ Applause ]

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.934
It comes with a hat.

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:51.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
We have a hat, too.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.734
Wow.
Okay.

00:00:53.734 --> 00:00:56.501
Wow.

00:00:56.501 --> 00:01:01.133
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:01:01.133 --> 00:01:02.667
Now let's see --

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:04.701
Now let's see who's going home
with tonight's sweater.

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:06.200
Everyone look
at your seat number.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.234
If I call your number -- if I
call your number, come on down.

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:11.200
Quest, could I get
a drumroll, please?

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.834
[ Drumroll ]

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:16.934
238!

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:18.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes! Come here!

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:19.667
Come on down.

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:27.934
♪♪

00:01:27.934 --> 00:01:29.567
Yes!

00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:31.267
Hello!
How you doing?

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:32.400
-Good. How are you?
-Nice to see you.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.501
You can stand over there.

00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:35.567
Hi.
What is your name?

00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:37.167
-Mikayla.
-Mikayla, where are you from?

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:38.567
-I'm from Nashville.
-Hey!

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:39.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:42.100
Nashville in the house!

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.334
It can get cool sometimes at
nighttime in Nashville, right?

00:01:44.334 --> 00:01:45.434
-Yep.
-Do you have anything

00:01:45.434 --> 00:01:47.334
like this at home?
-I don't think so.

00:01:47.334 --> 00:01:48.734
-How about the matching beanie?

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:49.901
Do you have anything like that?
-Nope.

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:51.300
-Would you like to try it on
for our audience?

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.868
-Oh, of course.
[ Cheers ]

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:55.267
-Do you want me to hold
your glasses or you got it?

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:57.334
You can han-- All right.
Mikayla, good job.

00:01:57.334 --> 00:01:58.634
Be careful.

00:01:58.634 --> 00:01:59.634
♪♪

00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:00.734
-Oh, perfect.

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:02.567
[ Cheers ]

00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:07.534
♪♪

00:02:07.534 --> 00:02:08.767
-There we go.

00:02:08.767 --> 00:02:11.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:14.133
-Thank you.

